### bashrs: what the exit code actually is, on BOTH sides
bashrs exits 1 whenever it has anything to say, errors or not, so the exit
code alone says nothing about this change. Measured on both:
  base (origin/main:scripts/quorum-gate.sh): Summary: 0 error(s), 11 warning(s), 41 info(s)
  head (this branch):                        Summary: 0 error(s), 15 warning(s), 46 info(s)
  both exit 1; ERRORS are 0 on both sides, which is the floor this repo holds.

The four warnings the arm adds, each one read:
  319 SC2101 [![:space:]]      — a case PATTERN, and [![:space:]] is the correct
                                 spelling of 'contains a non-space'. False positive.
  325 SC2086 $branch_id        — column 41-51 is INSIDE the die message's double
  331 SC2086 $branch_id          quotes; bashrs parses the multi-line string as code.
  327 BRS0023 read -r          — line 327 is the English word 'read' in the sentence
                                 'The branch name is read by gate A'. Same cause.
None is a shell defect; all four come from one multi-line quoted message.
